	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41904</id><title>Dialogue is ‘not naïve – it’s necessary’ as global divisions deepen, UN Riyadh forum hears</title><updated>2025-12-14T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41904" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/14-12-2025_SG_UNAOC2025.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/14-12-2025_SG_UNAOC2025.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The 11th Global Forum of the UN Alliance of Civilizations opened in Riyadh on Sunday with a blunt message for a world riven by distrust: dialogue is not a luxury – it’s a survival strategy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41904&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Dialogue is ‘not naïve – it’s necessary’ as global divisions deepen, UN Riyadh forum hears”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/14-12-2025_SG_UNAOC2025.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41903</id><title>Guterres condemns deadly attack on Hannukah celebration in Sydney</title><updated>2025-12-14T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41903" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/16-09-2025-UN_Photo-SG_PBR.jpeg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/16-09-2025-UN_Photo-SG_PBR.jpeg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;UN Secretary-General António Guterres has strongly condemned the “heinous deadly attack” on Sunday against Jewish families gathered in Sydney, Australia, to celebrate Hanukkah.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41903&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Guterres condemns deadly attack on Hannukah celebration in Sydney”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/16-09-2025-UN_Photo-SG_PBR.jpeg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41902</id><title>From farm to classroom: Feeding children and supporting farmers in Timor-Leste</title><updated>2025-12-14T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41902" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/11-12-2025-WFP-Timor-Leste-01.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/11-12-2025-WFP-Timor-Leste-01.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It’s a win-win recipe: schoolchildren eat a free, nutritious meal every day and local farmers gain reliable access to local markets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41902&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “From farm to classroom: Feeding children and supporting farmers in Timor-Leste”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/11-12-2025-WFP-Timor-Leste-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41899</id><title>UN marks first World Turkic Language Family Day</title><updated>2025-12-14T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41899" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/13-3-2025_Uzbekistan%20Samarkand%202.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/13-3-2025_Uzbekistan%20Samarkand%202.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The UN cultural agency, UNESCO, is preparing to celebrate the first ever World Turkic Language Family Day on Monday, following a decision by UNESCO’s General Conference in Samarkand to establish 15 December as an annual observance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/14/41899&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN marks first World Turkic Language Family Day”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/13-3-2025_Uzbekistan%20Samarkand%202.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41901</id><title>Sudan: UN strongly condemns deadly drone attack on peacekeeping base in Kordofan</title><updated>2025-12-13T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41901" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/06-11-2023-UN-Photo-UNMIS-peacekeeping.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/06-11-2023-UN-Photo-UNMIS-peacekeeping.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Drone attacks targeting the UN logistics base in Kadugli, Sudan, on Saturday killed six peacekeepers and injured eight others – all members of the Bangladeshi contingent serving in the UN Interim Security Force for Abyei (UNISFA).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41901&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Sudan: UN strongly condemns deadly drone attack on peacekeeping base in Kordofan”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/06-11-2023-UN-Photo-UNMIS-peacekeeping.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41900</id><title>In Baghdad, Guterres hails ‘new chapter’ in Iraq as UN mission draws to a close</title><updated>2025-12-13T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41900" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/13-12-25_SG_Iraq_2.jpeg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/13-12-25_SG_Iraq_2.jpeg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The United Nations Assistance Mission for Iraq (UNAMI) is ending operations this month but support for the country will continue, Secretary-General António Guterres affirmed at the official closing ceremony in Baghdad on Saturday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41900&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “In Baghdad, Guterres hails ‘new chapter’ in Iraq as UN mission draws to a close”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/13-12-25_SG_Iraq_2.jpeg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41898</id><title>With skills and determination, Guatemalans embark on life-changing journey to Germany</title><updated>2025-12-13T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41898" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/08-12-2025-IOM-Guatemala-01.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/08-12-2025-IOM-Guatemala-01.jpg/image1440x560cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On the runway of Guatemala City’s La Aurora International Airport, ten men embraced their families before departing for Germany — the start of a bold new chapter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41898&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “With skills and determination, Guatemalans embark on life-changing journey to Germany”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/08-12-2025-IOM-Guatemala-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41897</id><title>UN Alliance of Civilizations urges youth to reaffirm peace as a global priority</title><updated>2025-12-13T04:00:00-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41897" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/14-04-2025-UNICEF-Colombia.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/14-04-2025-UNICEF-Colombia.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In a world shaped by conflict and digital noise, the High Representative for the UN Alliance of Civilizations (UNAOC) called for young people to make the 21st century the last century in which humanity witnesses war.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/13/41897&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “UN Alliance of Civilizations urges youth to reaffirm peace as a global priority”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/14-04-2025-UNICEF-Colombia.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/12/41888</id><title>Sindh People’s Housing Redefines Post-Disaster Adaptation Success</title><updated>2025-12-12T08:58:09-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/12/41888" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/Sindhhousing-e1765528804689.jpeg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/Sindhhousing-e1765528804689.jpeg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
BELÉM, Brazil, December 12 (IPS)  - By any comparison, the statistics for Sindh People’s Housing for Flood Affectees (SPHF) are phenomenal.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/12/41888&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Sindh People’s Housing Redefines Post-Disaster Adaptation Success”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/Sindhhousing-e1765528804689-100x100.jpeg" width="100" height="100" /></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/12/41887</id><title>From Law to Lives Saved: How the Maternal Newborn and Child Health Bill Can Deliver Universal Health Coverage</title><updated>2025-12-12T06:28:20-08:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2025/12/12/41887" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/Health-workers-attend_.jpg" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2025/12/Health-workers-attend_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
